/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate27_vp_glycerol -- the vapour pressure of glycerol, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 and C283).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  glycerol`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to EVERY
  usable laboratory's measurements of it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1016/j.fluid.2015.03.038     113 pts  303.59-436.13 K  Verevkin; Zaitsau; Emel'yanenko; Zhabina
      10.1021/je200766t                11 pts  351.8-462.86 K  Mokbel; Sawaya; Zanota; Naccoul et al.
      10.1016/j.jct.2012.09.032         5 pts  477.25-520.65 K  Veneral; Benazzi; Mazutti; Voll et al.
      10.1021/je800070y                 5 pts  463.15-543.15 K  Yan; Suppes
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.jct.2013.09.046: 4 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.5b01080: 3 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  FIT AND GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, Vitor 2026-11-10; the evidence,
  objective and outliers of C283; declared before the fit).
  EVIDENCE: every study above is fitted; none is held out (C283 amended:
  laboratories disagree with each other by more than they claim, so the
  test is agreement across all of them, not one laboratory's claimed
  precision).  OBJECTIVE: `objective { method twoStage; }` -- least
  squares in log10 P for a first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in
  P, (P_model - P)/P, over the kept points minimised from it (Vitor's
  practice, C280); both answers kept.  OUTLIERS: after the least-squares
  stage a point with a relative P error above 15 % (three times
  the acceptance) is DISCARDED BY NAME (its study DOI, T and P), listed in
  the result and the record, and the fit repeated without it, once
  (`outliers { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }`).  ACCEPTANCE,
  GRADED, the DEFAULT of C285: the maximum relative P error over all kept
  points is graded clean up to 5 %, warning up to
  10 %, severe up to 20 % and refused above; where the
  normal-boiling-point condition below applies, the absolute gap is graded
  clean up to 1 K, warning up to 2 K, severe up to
  4 K and refused above.  The fit's grade is the WORSE of the
  two.  A clean, warning or severe fit is ACCEPTED and promoted (autoPromoted,
  humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade <grade>;` and the deciding numbers in
  its provenance entry, which the component loader voices on every run that
  uses it (a warning or a severe grade); a refused one is not promoted.  This
  case declares no `system/curationDict`, so the default applies; a case
  that needs another acceptance declares it there, with its reason.  The
  AmbroseWalton curve's errors on the same points are reported beside the
  fit's, as information.

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 563.15 K is judged against the range of the KEPT points (all studies span 303.59-543.15 K before any outlier is discarded): if Tb lies OUTSIDE that range, the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) is GRADED by its absolute gap to it (the temperature limits of the acceptance below); inside it, the gap is reported and is not a condition.

  EARLIER FITS, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 6.068473 - 2994.6061/(T + -63.1209),
  in-sample R2 0.999986 over 113 points, 303.59-436.13 K. HELD OUT: 11
  points, AAD 8.3035 % against the band 5 % -> notValidated. Its own
  normal boiling point (101.325 kPa): 557.06 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out
  verdict notValidated (AAD 8.303 % against the band 5 % declared before
  the fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton THEN C281 step 3, objective
  twoStage, one study fitted and one held out, judged by the band
  (superseded by C283): WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`;
  measured, not argued). Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) =
  5.889944 - 2876.5912/(T + -69.3990), in-sample R2 0.999928 over 113
  points, 303.59-436.13 K. HELD OUT: 11 points, AAD 6.9909 % (max 13.2871
  %) against the band 5 % -> notValidated; the stage-1 least-squares
  answer on the same points: AAD 8.3035 %, max 15.0182 %. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 558.26 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict
  notValidated (AAD 6.991 % against the band 5 % declared before the
  fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton. THEN C283, every usable study
  fitted and none held out, accepted only at max relative error <= 5 %
  and Tnb within 1 K (superseded by the graded acceptance of C285): WHAT
  THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued). Objective
  twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 5.808696 - 2818.0588/(T +
  -72.3003), in-sample R2 0.999561 over 134 kept points, 303.59-543.15 K
  (10.1016/j.fluid.2015.03.038 113/113 kept; 10.1021/je200766t 11/11
  kept; 10.1016/j.jct.2012.09.032 5/5 kept; 10.1021/je800070y 5/5 kept).
  Relative error in P over the kept points: mean 6.2927 %, max 8.6903 %;
  AmbroseWalton on the same points: mean 99.8560 %, max 100.0000 %.
  Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal boiling point (101.325 kPa):
  557.92 K. NOT PROMOTED by the DEFAULT acceptance of DEV.md 4c C283 (no
  system/curationDict): 4 studies, 134 points kept, 0 discarded as
  outliers; max relative error 8.69 % (mean 6.293 %) against 5 %;
  AmbroseWalton on the same points mean 99.86 % / max 100 %; the record
  keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares every
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 5.808696 - 2818.0588/(T +
  -72.3003), in-sample R2 0.999561 over 134 kept points, 303.59-543.15 K
  (10.1016/j.fluid.2015.03.038 113/113 kept; 10.1021/je200766t 11/11
  kept; 10.1016/j.jct.2012.09.032 5/5 kept; 10.1021/je800070y 5/5 kept).
  Relative error in P over the kept points: mean 6.2927 %, max 8.6903 %;
  AmbroseWalton on the same points: mean 99.8560 %, max 100.0000 %.
  Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal boiling point (101.325 kPa):
  557.92 K. NOT PROMOTED by the DEFAULT graded acceptance of DEV.md 4c
  C285 (no system/curationDict): fit grade refused -- 4 studies, 134
  points kept, 0 discarded as outliers; max relative error 8.69 % (mean
  6.293 %), grade warning (limits 5 / 10 / 20 %); Tb outside the kept
  points' range, normal boiling point 557.92 K, -5.23 K from the record's
  Tb 563.15 K, grade refused (limits 1 / 2 / 4 K); AmbroseWalton on the
  same points mean 99.86 % / max 100 %; the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  glycerol;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/glycerol-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2015.03.038.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2015.03.038"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/glycerol-vapourPressure-je200766t.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je200766t"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/glycerol-vapourPressure-j.jct.2012.09.032.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.jct.2012.09.032"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/glycerol-vapourPressure-je800070y.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je800070y"; }
                role      fit;
            }
        );

        objective  { method twoStage; }
        outliers   { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
